Upstream attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Lockin was developed from an engineering study of the Curbox Android
application:

    Project:  curbox-android
    URL:      https://github.com/curbox-app/curbox-android
    License:  GNU General Public License version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later)

In keeping with the GPL-3.0-or-later obligations that apply to derivative
works, Lockin:

  * is itself licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE),
  * credits the upstream project here and in README.md,
  * distributes its complete corresponding source (dist/Lockin-source.zip,
    and this repository), and
  * documents the changes made relative to the upstream study.

Notable modifications relative to the upstream project:

  * complete rebrand to Lockin with application id `com.rrrtx.lockin`,
  * original visual identity (hourglass mark, wordmark, light/dark design
    system) created for this project,
  * rewritten Kotlin codebase and redesigned user interface (onboarding,
    session dashboard, selection, commitment, blocker, history, schedules,
    settings, protection center),
  * strict session state machine with no early-unlock surface,
  * offline-first packaging: no network permission, no accounts, no analytics,
  * compatibility floor lowered to Android 6.0 (API 23) with version-aware
    compatibility handling,
  * expanded documentation set, tests, and verification scripts.

No source code from the upstream project is copied into this repository;
the upstream project informed architecture, threat modelling, and the
engineering checklist only. All code in this repository is original and
covered by this repository's GPL-3.0-or-later license.
